# The runtime-solver build stamp. `.maxnum-*` was ignored and its sibling was not, so `.maxnumrt-13`
# reached master in d5b06b9 — an empty file whose only job is to tell make whether eu_solver_rt was
# built at the current MAXNUM, and which `make clean` deletes.
.maxnumrt-*
# Ad-hoc palette-slice runs: <tag>-k<N>/ holding out/ plus a one-line solver log. The out/ tree is
# already ignored; these are the wrappers around it, hundreds of MB, regenerable via
# `PALETTE=<name> ./run-oracle.sh <k>`. What survives a run is the log in experiments/results/.
hollow-k*/
mid-k*/
oct-k*/
sq-k*/
eu_sphfill
# The runtime-table pruner, eu_solver_rt's companion (Makefile `eu_pruner_rt`). Same rule as the
# solver binaries in the root .gitignore: compiled, regenerable, never committed.
eu_pruner_rt
# Search and develop output of the 2026-08 curved runs, by palette tag: the isotoxal sweeps
# (iso-k*, im-k*, ip-k*, iw-k*, cmp-isotox-*, pair5-6, k3-*, k4-*, sweep-size*), the toroid probes
# (toroid-*), the rhombic bubble mixtures and the paused star-wide k=2 develop. Between 40 KB and
# 24 GB each, all regenerable via `PALETTE=<name> ./run-oracle-pool.sh <k>` plus the developer, and
# every solid worth keeping out of them is spliced into a tracked table under lib/render/. Same rule
# as sph-k3/ in the root .gitignore. The logs that record the runs live in experiments/results/.
cmp-isotox-*/
im-k*/
ip-k*/
iso-k*/
iw-k*/
k3-*/
k4-*/
pair5-6/
sweep-size*/
sweep*.log
toroid-*/
bubble-rhombic/
star-wide-k2-euclid-parts/
keep-verified/
# A develop output that sits bare in this directory instead of under a run dir. gen_nonconvex_shelf.py
# reads it as a sixth --cells file (DEFAULT_CELLS); ignored for the reason the sph-k*/ cells are.
star-ico-k2-euclid.json
# Harvest intermediates on the way to lib/render/{genusSolids,hemiSolids,isotoxalSolids}.ts and the
# spherical atlas rows — genus_harvest.py, gen_genus_shelf.py, gen_hemi_shelf.py, gen_isotoxal_shelf.py
# write these and scripts/build-*-shelf.mjs read them. Same rule as nonconvex-rows.json.
genus-rows.json
genus-atlas-rows.json
hemi-atlas-rows.json
isotoxal-atlas-rows.json
